  "_comment": [
    "THE RELEASE INDEX LIVES OUTSIDE EVERY RELEASE. A frozen release cannot list",
    "the releases that come after it, so this file sits beside them — typically at",
    "the install root, one level above the version directories.",
    "",
    "It is UNTRUSTED INPUT, in the same category as an installed adapter. An entry",
    "is a CLAIM that a release sits at a path; `tools/pack_migration.py` is what",
    "verifies the claim against the release itself before offering it. An entry",
    "missing any required field is REFUSED, never skipped: a skipped entry makes",
    "the index describe fewer releases than it lists, silently.",
    "",
    "EACH VERSION MUST RESOLVE TO ITS OWN IMMUTABLE ROOT (DECISIONS.md D13).",
    "Paths are canonicalised before comparison, so two entries cannot reach the",
    "same directory through a symlink. One directory moved between revisions makes",
    "every pin to it unverifiable at once — which is the failure D13 exists to",
    "prevent, and it is reproducible: a release root that is also somebody's",
    "working tree stops verifying the moment a branch is checked out in it.",
    "",
    "So a release root is a checkout NOBODY WORKS IN. Evolution happens somewhere",
    "else, and a new version becomes a release by being placed at a new root and",
    "added here.",
    "",
    "`security_advisory` is disclosed loudly and AUTHORISES NOTHING. Urgency is a",
    "reason for a person to decide sooner, never a reason to skip the capability",
    "boundary or the human (policy/hitl-matrix.md)."
